<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25009" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrŭbesco</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ), bŭi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i> [in-rubesco], <i>to grow red</i>, <i>be reddened</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec sanguine ferrum irrubuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 6, 231</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">9, 647</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">haemachates sanguineis maculis irrubescit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 5, 27</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To throw a red light</i> upon a thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tuis ut mihi vultibus ignis irrubuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 3, 32</span></i>
			.</div>
